<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eugippius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 465–c. 533</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eugippius was a monk and disciple of Saint Severinus, who left Noricum with the Roman population in 488 and became abbot of a monastery near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. Around 511 he wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/life-of-saint-severinus">Life of Saint Severinus</a>, a vivid account of the last years of Roman rule on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. It is the main source for the Rugians and their kings.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Eugippius</b>' Life of Saint Severinus portrays King Flaccitheus, his son Feletheus and the harsh Queen Giso, whom the saint rebuked.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-the-rugians">Kingdom of the Rugians</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Castel dell'Ovo, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.83,14.25&amp;year=509" aria-label="Castel dell'Ovo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4899 706 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Eugippius"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5349 976h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5349 976h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=40.83,14.25&amp;year=509">What was here in 509 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
